# Architecture Boundaries

- Keep Web and Mobile as clients; external traffic enters through API Gateway.
- Preserve service ownership: User, Content, Learning, AI, and Analytics own separate domains.
- Each business service owns its API, business logic, Prisma schema, and PostgreSQL database.
- Do not add shared databases, shared Prisma clients, or shared business-logic packages.
- Put code in the service that owns the domain; coordinate through explicit APIs or events.
- Update `docs/architecture/` when a service boundary or communication path changes.
